# Vue 3 + TypeScript Standards

## Vue 3 Composition API

Use Vue 3 Composition API with `<script setup>` syntax as shown in [resources/js/pages/Dashboard.vue](mdc:resources/js/pages/Dashboard.vue):

- Use `<script setup lang="ts">` for TypeScript support
- Define props and emits with TypeScript interfaces
- Use `withDefaults()` for default prop values

## TypeScript Interfaces

Define proper interfaces for props and emits:

```typescript
interface Props {
  title: string
  count?: number
}

interface Emits {
  (e: 'update', value: string): void
}
```

## Component Structure

Follow the pattern in [resources/js/components/AppShell.vue](mdc:resources/js/components/AppShell.vue):

- Use PascalCase for component names
- Use PascalCase for component file names
- Implement proper TypeScript typing
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling, with shadcn/ui components

## Inertia.js Integration

Components should work with Inertia.js as shown in [resources/js/app.ts](mdc:resources/js/app.ts):

- Use Inertia's shared data for global state
- Handle Inertia events properly
- Implement proper error boundaries

## TypeScript Configuration

Follow the configuration in [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json):

- Enable strict type checking
- Use proper module resolution
- Include Vue file types
- Set up path aliases for clean imports

## UI Components

Use the UI component library in [resources/js/components/ui/](mdc:resources/js/components/ui/):

- Follow the established component patterns
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces
- Implement accessibility features
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
